## Overview

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Base URL** | `https://api.example.com` |
| **Auth** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |
| **Rate limit** | 100 requests / second per token |

:::tip Idempotency
Send an `Idempotency-Key` (UUID) with every `POST`. Retrying with the same key and body returns the original response, so mobile clients can retry safely.
:::

## Endpoints

:::api{method=POST path="/v1/orders" auth="bearer token"} Create an order
| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `items` | LineItem[] | yes | At least one item |
| `country` | string | yes | ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 |
| `coupon` | string | no | Invalid coupons return `422` with `fields.coupon` |

**Responses:** `201` order · `402` payment declined · `409` idempotency key reused with a different body · `422` validation errors (all fields at once)
:::

:::api{method=GET path="/v1/orders/{id}" auth="bearer token"} Get an order
**Responses:** `200` order · `404` not found
:::

:::api{method=POST path="/v1/orders/{id}/cancel" auth="bearer token"} Cancel an order
Only orders in `pending` or `paid` state can be cancelled; paid orders are refunded.

**Responses:** `200` cancelled order · `409` order already shipped
:::

## Pricing logic

Prices are integer cents. The API uses the shared pricing module (lines 7–13 highlighted):

```ts file="src/pricing.ts" lines="1-17" {7-13}
```

## Errors

| Status | Meaning | Retry? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `401` | Missing or invalid token | No |
| `409` | Conflict (see endpoint) | No |
| `429` | Rate limited | Yes, after `Retry-After` |
| `5xx` | Server error | Yes, with exponential backoff and the same idempotency key |

